A||N||3||rforbes||Roller lifters in a '84??||||5||
Z||000000||rforbes||02-15-2001||09:10 AM||||I recently bought a "dead" '84 with a 2.5 and automatic.  The engine had a hole in one piston so I am rebuilding it.  My question is:  Were there any '84 2.5s with roller cams?  I have been told no but when I tore mine down, it is. Where do I find the casting numbers and what do I look for to know what year engine I have??  I am looking forward to getting this car on the road and any help will be greatly appreciated.<P>Rodney||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||02-15-2001||01:36 PM||||The engine may have been replaced during one of the recalls. My 84 got a new engine as part of the "fire" recall and the new one came with roller lifters.  It also has the crankshaft with the gear to drive the balance shafts that appeared on the later 4 cylinders. All of the parts you need for rebuild (gaskets, rings, bearings and such) are the same as the ones in the original engine.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Rodrv6 (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000002||theogre||02-15-2001||07:40 PM||||GM documents show that "as built" no 84 had roller lifters. This one was very likely a motor replaced thru recall. This is a good thing. The roller cam is likely in good shape. These also put less load on timing gears.<P>Make sure all the lifters, push rods, etc, go back in the spots they came from when you put the thing together again. Roller cams are still craby about that but not like flat tappets.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rforbes||02-16-2001||09:11 AM||||Thanks for the info.  This car has been sitting with the head off for quite a while - I'm not sure how long, it was off when I bought the car, so I am afraid the lifters might stick.  Therefore, I am buying a complete re-build kit that includes cam and lifters, pistons - I'm having it bored .030 over, oil pump etc.  I just wanted to make sure the parts house got the right stuff for me.  I also plan to go through the auto tranny before it goes back under the car.  After that, a little paint and clean up the interior and I should have a decent ride for a small price.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Maybe some day I'll get a newer one and drop in a V8!||||reg||6
